<ContentLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Fix The Speaker"
  description="Privacy policy for Fix The Speaker, the free phone speaker cleaner. Learn what data is collected, how cookies and ads work, and your choices."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  updated="2026-09-03"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what information Fix The Speaker (<a href="https://fixthespeaker.com">fixthespeaker.com</a>)
    collects, how it is used and the choices you have. The short version: the tool itself collects nothing, and the
    only data processing comes from standard hosting logs, analytics and advertising services.
  </p>

  <h2>Information the tool processes</h2>
  <p>
    The speaker cleaning tool runs entirely in your browser. Sound is generated on your device with the Web Audio API.
    We do not record audio, request microphone access, create accounts, or ask you to enter any personal information to
    use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
  <p>
    Like most websites, our hosting provider records basic technical data in server logs, such as your IP address,
    browser type, referring page, pages visited and timestamps. This data is used to keep the site secure and
    available and is retained only for as long as needed for that purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We may use Google Analytics to understand how visitors use the site, for example which pages are popular and which
    devices are common. Google Analytics uses cookies and collects information such as your approximate location,
    device and interactions in an aggregated form. You can opt out with the
    <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google AdSense to display advertising. Google and its partners use cookies, including the DoubleClick
    cookie, to serve ads based on your prior visits to this and other websites. You can opt out of personalized
    advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>
    or <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a>. Third-party vendors may
    also use cookies to serve ads; their use of data is governed by their own privacy policies.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. The speaker cleaning tool works with cookies disabled.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    The site loads fonts from Google Fonts and may embed scripts from Google Analytics and Google AdSense. Each of
    these services may receive your IP address and browser information when the resource is requested. Their
    processing is described in the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct or delete personal data held about you, or
    to object to certain processing. Because we do not hold personal data ourselves, most requests should be directed
    to the third-party services above. For anything else, <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of the page shows when it was last revised.
    Continued use of the site after a change means you accept the updated policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy can be sent through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.</p>
</ContentLayout>
